<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Deep neural networks have demonstrated exceptional performance across different machine learning applications.<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">LeCun et al., 2015</a>)</cite> One of the fundamental methodologies of deep learning involves overparameterized models. These networks are highly expressive and are often easy to optimize to (near) zero training error with SGD. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mingard et al., 2025</a>)</cite> In many settings, making the model even larger can improve test performance beyond the interpolation threshold, a phenomenon also known as double descent.<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nakkiran et al., 2019</a>)</cite>. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bubeck et al., 2021</a>)</cite> provide a theoretical explanation for why overparameterization is necessary. They introduce a sharp law of robustness for two layer neural networks showing that achieving robust interpolation characterized by a small Lipschitz constant requires more parameters than interpolation alone. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bubeck and Sellke, 2021</a>)</cite> then prove a universal version under isoperimetric covariate distributions, showing that smooth interpolation for <math id="S1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> Lipschitz requires <math id="S1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\gg nd" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≫</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\gg nd</annotation></semantics></math> parameters. Furthermore, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2023</a>)</cite> extend the theory beyond isoperimetry, providing robust-interpolation lower bounds for arbitrary bounded-support distribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Despite their remarkable success, deep networks remain vulnerable to subtle perturbations, as revealed through the existence of adversarial samples. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Goodfellow et al., 2015</a>)</cite>
The most common mitigation strategy is adversarial training, where models are trained on adversarially perturbed examples to improve robustness. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shafahi et al., 2019</a>)</cite> Furthermore, methods such as margin-based measures, flatness-based measures, and gradient-based measures have also been utilized to improve adverserial robustness. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Scaman and Virmaux, 2019</a>)</cite>
Another line of work pursues certified robustness by constraining the Lipschitz constant of the model, which provides formal guarantees on the maximum possible perturbation impact. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al., 2023</a>)</cite></p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">However, none of these methods explicitly connect overparameterization and Lipschitz constant constraints to robust generalization, the gap between robust training and robust test performance. This is what Bubeck and Selke in their 2021 paper refer to as a "fantastic open problem." In this work, we solve it and make the following contributions:</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">1) We theoretically lower bound the robust generalization gap.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">2) We decompose the robust loss and derive an upper bound using Rademacher complexity; we further establish this in a distribution-free setting and recover Wu et al.’s <math id="S1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(n^{1/d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(n^{1/d})</annotation></semantics></math> lower bound, demonstrating that the Lipschitz constant must lie within a specific range.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">3) We empirically test both <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al. (2023)</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bubeck et al., 2021</a>)</cite> bounds using MNIST and evaluate how well they align with the empirical lower bound on the Lipschitz constant.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Related Work</h2>

<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1 </span>Adversarial robustness, adversarial training, and Lipschitz</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Modern neural networks are vulnerable to <em id="S2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">adversarial examples</em>, a phenomenon first identified by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Szegedy et al., 2013</a>; <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Goodfellow et al., 2014</a>)</cite>
The most widely used defense is <em id="S2.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">adversarial training</em>, which minimizes a worst-case objective over bounded perturbations <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Madry et al., 2018</a>)</cite>, with principled variants such as TRADES making explicit the trade-off between standard and robust accuracy <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2019</a>)</cite>.
Furthermore, parameter-free evaluation suites such as AutoAttack are commonly used for reliable comparison due to robustness being highly sensitive to the threat model
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Croce and Hein, 2020</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Another line of work deals <em id="S2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">certified robustness</em> by controlling (global or local) Lipschitz.
Bounding a model’s Lipschitz constant yields worst-case guarantees on output variation under input
perturbations, motivating Lipschitz regularization and Lipschitz-constrained architectures. Examples such as Parseval networks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cissé et al., 2017</a>)</cite>, Lipschitz-margin training
for scalable certification <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tsuzuku et al., 2018</a>)</cite>, and more recent work emphasizing
expressive Lipschitz networks for improved certified robustness <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2022</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">However, computing tight global Lipschitz constants for deep neural networks is difficult, so much work has focused on computable bounds and approximations.
CLEVER relates robustness evaluation to local Lipschitz estimation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Weng et al., 2018</a>)</cite>, while
optimization-based methods provide tighter upper bounds for neural networks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fazlyab et al., 2019</a>)</cite>.
Moreover,<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zühlke and Kudenko, 2025</a>)</cite> provides a comprehensive survey unifying Lipschitz constants, adversarial attacks, robustness guarantees, and estimation methods.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2 </span>Overparameterization and laws of robustness</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recent theory connects <em id="S2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">model size</em> and <em id="S2.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">smooth interpolation</em> through lower bounds on the
Lipschitz constant of interpolating predictors.
Bubeck, Li, and Nagaraj formulate and prove a sharp trade-off for two-layer networks, suggesting that
overparameterization is necessary to achieve small Lipschitz constant while fitting the data
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bubeck et al., 2021</a>)</cite>.
Bubeck and Sellke establish a <em id="S2.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">universal</em> version under isoperimetric-type covariate distributions,
showing that smooth interpolation can require substantially more parameters than interpolation alone
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bubeck and Sellke, 2021</a>)</cite>.
Wu, Huang, and Zhang extend this direction beyond isoperimetry and derive distribution-free
robust-interpolation lower bounds, including an <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega(n^{1/d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega(n^{1/d})</annotation></semantics></math> regime for general bounded-support
distributions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.
More recently, Das, Batra, and Srivastava generalize universal-law-type results beyond squared loss to
a broad family of Bregman divergence losses (covering common classification losses)
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Das et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, and related work also studies robustness laws under weight-bounded classes
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Husain and Balle, 2021</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.3 </span>Robust generalization and robust overfitting</h3>

<div id="S2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A persistent challenge in adversarial robustness is robust generalization, where robust training error can be low while test error remains high.
It is known that robust learning can require significantly more labeled data than standard learning, even in simple data models
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schmidt et al., 2018</a>)</cite>. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Carmon et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhai et al., 2019</a>)</cite>.
It has also been shown by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yin et al., 2019</a>)</cite> that robust generalization bounds exhibit unavoidable dimension dependence unless additional structure is imposed.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A closely related phenomenon is <em id="S2.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">robust overfitting</em>: continued adversarial training can improve
robust training loss while degrading robust test performance.
Rice, Wong, and Kolter document robust overfitting across datasets and show that early stopping can
match many improvements attributed to algorithmic tweaks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rice et al., 2020</a>)</cite>.
Subsequent work proposes mechanisms to mitigate robust overfitting via learned smoothing
regularization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2021</a>)</cite> or by analyzing which subsets of adversarial examples drive
overfitting and modifying training to counteract it <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu et al., 2022</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Morever, it has recently been shown why why robust generalization is intrinsically challenging from an expressive
power perspective <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2022</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, several recent papers develop stability-based and training-dynamics-based explanations for
robust generalization behavior <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2024a</a>)</cite>
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cheng et al., 2024</a>)</cite><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2024b</a>)</cite>.
Additionally, recent work further formalizes the clean-generalization vs. robust-overfitting dichotomy through
representation complexity and phase-transition analyses <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li and Li, 2025</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Lower Bound on Robust Generalization Gap</h2>

<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Robust–clean empirical gap)<span id="Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz with respect to a norm <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f(x)-f(x^{\prime})|\leq L\|x-x^{\prime}\|\quad\text{for all }x,x^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f(x)-f(x^{\prime})|\leq L\|x-x^{\prime}\|\quad\text{for all }x,x^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and training samples <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(x_{i},y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(x_{i},y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define the <em id="Thmlemma1.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">clean</em> empirical (train) error</span></p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{R}:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\bigl(f(x_{i})-y_{i}\bigr)^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{R}:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\bigl(f(x_{i})-y_{i}\bigr)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and the <em id="Thmlemma1.p1.3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">robust</em> empirical (train) error</span></p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sup_{\|\delta\|&lt;\rho}\bigl(f(x_{i}+\delta)-y_{i}\bigr)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R:=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sup_{\|\delta\|&lt;\rho}\bigl(f(x_{i}+\delta)-y_{i}\bigr)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then</span></p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R-\widehat{R}\leq 2L\rho\sqrt{\widehat{R}}+L^{2}\rho^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R-\widehat{R}\leq 2L\rho\sqrt{\widehat{R}}+L^{2}\rho^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}:=f(x_{i})-y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}:=f(x_{i})-y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\delta\|&lt;\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\delta\|&lt;\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, the Lipschitz property gives</span></p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f(x_{i}+\delta)-f(x_{i})|\leq L\|x_{i}+\delta-x_{i}\|=L\|\delta\|\leq L\rho." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f(x_{i}+\delta)-f(x_{i})|\leq L\|x_{i}+\delta-x_{i}\|=L\|\delta\|\leq L\rho.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">By the triangle inequality,</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|f(x_{i}+\delta)-y_{i}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|f(x_{i}+\delta)-y_{i}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq|f(x_{i}+\delta)-f(x_{i})|+|f(x_{i})-y_{i}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq|f(x_{i}+\delta)-f(x_{i})|+|f(x_{i})-y_{i}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq L\rho+|r_{i}|," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq L\rho+|r_{i}|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">where we used (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In Proof. ‣ 3 Lower Bound on Robust Generalization Gap ‣ Does Order Matter : Connecting The Law of Robustness to Robust Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) in the last step. Squaring and taking the supremum over <math id="S3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\delta\|&lt;\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\delta\|&lt;\rho</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{\|\delta\|&lt;\rho}\bigl(f(x_{i}+\delta)-y_{i}\bigr)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{\|\delta\|&lt;\rho}\bigl(f(x_{i}+\delta)-y_{i}\bigr)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(L\rho+|r_{i}|)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(L\rho+|r_{i}|)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=L^{2}\rho^{2}+2L\rho|r_{i}|+r_{i}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=L^{2}\rho^{2}+2L\rho|r_{i}|+r_{i}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Averaging (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In Proof. ‣ 3 Lower Bound on Robust Generalization Gap ‣ Does Order Matter : Connecting The Law of Robustness to Robust Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) over <math id="S3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\leq\widehat{R}+\frac{2L\rho}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}|r_{i}|+L^{2}\rho^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\leq\widehat{R}+\frac{2L\rho}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}|r_{i}|+L^{2}\rho^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, by Cauchy–Schwarz,</span></p>
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}|r_{i}|\leq\sqrt{\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}r_{i}^{2}}=\sqrt{\widehat{R}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}|r_{i}|\leq\sqrt{\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}r_{i}^{2}}=\sqrt{\widehat{R}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting (<a href="#S3.E8" title="In Proof. ‣ 3 Lower Bound on Robust Generalization Gap ‣ Does Order Matter : Connecting The Law of Robustness to Robust Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) into (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In Proof. ‣ 3 Lower Bound on Robust Generalization Gap ‣ Does Order Matter : Connecting The Law of Robustness to Robust Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) yields (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In Lemma 1 (Robust–clean empirical gap). ‣ 3 Lower Bound on Robust Generalization Gap ‣ Does Order Matter : Connecting The Law of Robustness to Robust Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now translate the robust generalization gap <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T-R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-R</annotation></semantics></math> into a lower bound on the
<em id="S3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">expected</em> Rademacher complexity using Eq. (1) of Wu et al. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">wu2022law</span>)</cite>.
To avoid a clash with the adversarial perturbation <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S3.E2" title="In Lemma 1 (Robust–clean empirical gap). ‣ 3 Lower Bound on Robust Generalization Gap ‣ Does Order Matter : Connecting The Law of Robustness to Robust Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>),
we denote the confidence parameter by <math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathrm{conf}}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathrm{conf}}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout this subsection, assume <math id="S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\in[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\in[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely and that <math id="S3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="S3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz. Define the robust squared loss</p>
<table id="S3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\rho}(f;(x,y))\coloneqq\sup_{\left\lVert\delta\right\rVert\leq\rho}\bigl(f(x+\delta)-y\bigr)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\rho}(f;(x,y))\coloneqq\sup_{\left\lVert\delta\right\rVert\leq\rho}\bigl(f(x+\delta)-y\bigr)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz, for any <math id="S3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\delta\right\rVert\leq\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\delta\right\rVert\leq\rho</annotation></semantics></math> we have</p>
<table id="S3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f(x+\delta)-y|\leq|f(x)-y|+|f(x+\delta)-f(x)|\leq 2+L\rho," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f(x+\delta)-y|\leq|f(x)-y|+|f(x+\delta)-f(x)|\leq 2+L\rho,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">and hence the robust loss is uniformly bounded by</p>
<table id="S3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\ell_{\rho}(f;(X,Y))\leq(2+L\rho)^{2}\eqqcolon a_{\rho}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≕</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\ell_{\rho}(f;(X,Y))\leq(2+L\rho)^{2}\eqqcolon a_{\rho}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Applying Eq. (1) of Wu et al. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_citation ltx_ref_self">wu2022law</span>)</cite> to the bounded loss <math id="S3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>
yields that, with probability at least <math id="S3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta_{\mathrm{conf}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta_{\mathrm{conf}}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\sim D^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\sim D^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>,
for all <math id="S3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> in the class,</p>
<table id="S3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T-R\leq 2\,\mathbb{E}_{S^{\prime}\sim D^{n}}\!\left[\mathfrak{R}\!\bigl(\ell_{\rho}\circ\mathcal{F}\circ S^{\prime}\bigr)\right]+a_{\rho}\sqrt{\frac{2\ln(2/\delta_{\mathrm{conf}})}{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.552em;" width="0.552em"><mi>ℜ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-R\leq 2\,\mathbb{E}_{S^{\prime}\sim D^{n}}\!\left[\mathfrak{R}\!\bigl(\ell_{\rho}\circ\mathcal{F}\circ S^{\prime}\bigr)\right]+a_{\rho}\sqrt{\frac{2\ln(2/\delta_{\mathrm{conf}})}{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Consequently, whenever <math id="S3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T-R\geq\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T-R\geq\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{S^{\prime}\sim D^{n}}\!\left[\mathfrak{R}\!\bigl(\ell_{\rho}\circ\mathcal{F}\circ S^{\prime}\bigr)\right]\geq\frac{\gamma}{2}-\frac{a_{\rho}}{2}\sqrt{\frac{2\ln(2/\delta_{\mathrm{conf}})}{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.552em;" width="0.552em"><mi>ℜ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{S^{\prime}\sim D^{n}}\!\left[\mathfrak{R}\!\bigl(\ell_{\rho}\circ\mathcal{F}\circ S^{\prime}\bigr)\right]\geq\frac{\gamma}{2}-\frac{a_{\rho}}{2}\sqrt{\frac{2\ln(2/\delta_{\mathrm{conf}})}{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In particular, under Assumption <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>, Corollary <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span> gives
<math id="S3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\varepsilon-(2L\rho\sigma+L^{2}\rho^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\varepsilon-(2L\rho\sigma+L^{2}\rho^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, so</p>
<table id="S3.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{S^{\prime}\sim D^{n}}\!\left[\mathfrak{R}\!\bigl(\ell_{\rho}\circ\mathcal{F}\circ S^{\prime}\bigr)\right]\geq\frac{\varepsilon-(2L\rho\sigma+L^{2}\rho^{2})}{2}-\frac{a_{\rho}}{2}\sqrt{\frac{2\ln(2/\delta_{\mathrm{conf}})}{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.552em;" width="0.552em"><mi>ℜ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{S^{\prime}\sim D^{n}}\!\left[\mathfrak{R}\!\bigl(\ell_{\rho}\circ\mathcal{F}\circ S^{\prime}\bigr)\right]\geq\frac{\varepsilon-(2L\rho\sigma+L^{2}\rho^{2})}{2}-\frac{a_{\rho}}{2}\sqrt{\frac{2\ln(2/\delta_{\mathrm{conf}})}{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Local extremal envelopes</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{X},\left\lVert\cdot\right\rVert)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{X},\left\lVert\cdot\right\rVert)</annotation></semantics></math> be a normed vector space and fix <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Local extremal envelopes)<span id="Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="S4.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{+}(x)\coloneqq\sup_{\left\lVert\delta\right\rVert\leq\rho}f(x+\delta),\qquad f^{-}(x)\coloneqq\inf_{\left\lVert\delta\right\rVert\leq\rho}f(x+\delta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{+}(x)\coloneqq\sup_{\left\lVert\delta\right\rVert\leq\rho}f(x+\delta),\qquad f^{-}(x)\coloneqq\inf_{\left\lVert\delta\right\rVert\leq\rho}f(x+\delta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Envelopes preserve Lipschitzness)<span id="Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz, then both <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,x^{\prime}\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,x^{\prime}\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f^{+}(x)-f^{+}(x^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f^{+}(x)-f^{+}(x^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sup_{\left\lVert\delta\right\rVert\leq\rho}f(x+\delta)-\sup_{\left\lVert\delta\right\rVert\leq\rho}f(x^{\prime}+\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sup_{\left\lVert\delta\right\rVert\leq\rho}f(x+\delta)-\sup_{\left\lVert\delta\right\rVert\leq\rho}f(x^{\prime}+\delta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sup_{\left\lVert\delta\right\rVert\leq\rho}\bigl(f(x+\delta)-f(x^{\prime}+\delta)\bigr)\leq\sup_{\left\lVert\delta\right\rVert\leq\rho}L\left\lVert x-x^{\prime}\right\rVert=L\left\lVert x-x^{\prime}\right\rVert." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sup_{\left\lVert\delta\right\rVert\leq\rho}\bigl(f(x+\delta)-f(x^{\prime}+\delta)\bigr)\leq\sup_{\left\lVert\delta\right\rVert\leq\rho}L\left\lVert x-x^{\prime}\right\rVert=L\left\lVert x-x^{\prime}\right\rVert.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Swapping the roles of <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> yields <math id="S4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f^{+}(x)-f^{+}(x^{\prime})|\leq L\left\lVert x-x^{\prime}\right\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f^{+}(x)-f^{+}(x^{\prime})|\leq L\left\lVert x-x^{\prime}\right\rVert</annotation></semantics></math>.
The proof for <math id="S4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> is identical.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Robust squared loss)<span id="Thmdefinition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)\in\mathcal{X}\times\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="S4.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\rho}(f;(x,y))\coloneqq\sup_{\left\lVert\delta\right\rVert\leq\rho}(f(x+\delta)-y)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\rho}(f;(x,y))\coloneqq\sup_{\left\lVert\delta\right\rVert\leq\rho}(f(x+\delta)-y)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Worst-case squared deviation is at an endpoint)<span id="Thmlemma3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f,x,y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f,x,y</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\rho}(f;(x,y))=\max\Bigl\{(f^{+}(x)-y)^{2},\ (f^{-}(x)-y)^{2}\Bigr\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\rho}(f;(x,y))=\max\Bigl\{(f^{+}(x)-y)^{2},\ (f^{-}(x)-y)^{2}\Bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The set of attainable values <math id="S4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{f(x+\delta):\left\lVert\delta\right\rVert\leq\rho\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{f(x+\delta):\left\lVert\delta\right\rVert\leq\rho\}</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in the interval
<math id="S4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[f^{-}(x),f^{+}(x)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[f^{-}(x),f^{+}(x)]</annotation></semantics></math>. The map <math id="S4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\mapsto(z-y)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\mapsto(z-y)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is convex, hence it attains its maximum over a
compact interval at an endpoint. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\left\lVert\delta\right\rVert\leq\rho}(f(x+\delta)-y)^{2}=\max_{z\in[f^{-}(x),f^{+}(x)]}(z-y)^{2}=\max\{(f^{+}(x)-y)^{2},(f^{-}(x)-y)^{2}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\left\lVert\delta\right\rVert\leq\rho}(f(x+\delta)-y)^{2}=\max_{z\in[f^{-}(x),f^{+}(x)]}(z-y)^{2}=\max\{(f^{+}(x)-y)^{2},(f^{-}(x)-y)^{2}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Rademacher complexity for loss vectors</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=(\sigma_{1},\dots,\sigma_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=(\sigma_{1},\dots,\sigma_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> be i.i.d. Rademacher signs, i.e. <math id="S5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lx@paragraphsign(\sigma_{i}=1)=\lx@paragraphsign(\sigma_{i}=-1)=\tfrac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>¶</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>¶</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lx@paragraphsign(\sigma_{i}=1)=\lx@paragraphsign(\sigma_{i}=-1)=\tfrac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Empirical Rademacher complexity of a set of vectors)<span id="Thmdefinition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a set <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="S5.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(A)\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{\sigma}\left[\sup_{a\in A}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}a_{i}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(A)\coloneqq\mathbb{E}_{\sigma}\left[\sup_{a\in A}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}a_{i}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 1</span></span><span id="Thmremark1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The normalizing factor <math id="Thmremark1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is conventional. All inequalities below are homogeneous in that
factor, so any consistent convention works.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We will use the following basic properties repeatedly.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="Thmlemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Translations and Minkowski sums)<span id="Thmlemma4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be fixed.</span></p>
<ol id="S5.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(</span><em id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph">Translation invariance</em><span id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) </span><math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(A+c)=\mathfrak{R}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(A+c)=\mathfrak{R}(A)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(</span><em id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph">Subadditivity</em><span id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) </span><math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(A+B)\leq\mathfrak{R}(A)+\mathfrak{R}(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(A+B)\leq\mathfrak{R}(A)+\mathfrak{R}(B)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, where </span><math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A+B\coloneqq\{a+b:a\in A,b\in B\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A+B\coloneqq\{a+b:a\in A,b\in B\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(</span><em id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph">Difference bound</em><span id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">) </span><math id="S5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(A-B)\leq\mathfrak{R}(A)+\mathfrak{R}(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(A-B)\leq\mathfrak{R}(A)+\mathfrak{R}(B)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, where </span><math id="S5.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A-B\coloneqq\{a-b:a\in A,b\in B\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A-B\coloneqq\{a-b:a\in A,b\in B\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">For (a), for each realization of <math id="S5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{a\in A}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}(a_{i}+c_{i})=\sup_{a\in A}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}a_{i}+\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}c_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{a\in A}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}(a_{i}+c_{i})=\sup_{a\in A}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}a_{i}+\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}c_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectations over <math id="S5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, the last term vanishes since <math id="S5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\sigma_{i}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\sigma_{i}]=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For (b), for each <math id="S5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{a\in A,\ b\in B}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}(a_{i}+b_{i})\leq\sup_{a\in A}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}a_{i}+\sup_{b\in B}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}b_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{a\in A,\ b\in B}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}(a_{i}+b_{i})\leq\sup_{a\in A}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}a_{i}+\sup_{b\in B}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}b_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectations gives the claim.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For (c), similarly,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{a\in A,\ b\in B}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}(a_{i}-b_{i})=\sup_{a\in A}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}a_{i}+\sup_{b\in B}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(-\sigma_{i})b_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{a\in A,\ b\in B}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}(a_{i}-b_{i})=\sup_{a\in A}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}a_{i}+\sup_{b\in B}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(-\sigma_{i})b_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-\sigma_{1},\dots,-\sigma_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-\sigma_{1},\dots,-\sigma_{n})</annotation></semantics></math> has the same law as <math id="S5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, the expectation of the second
supremum is <math id="S5.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(B)</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding <math id="S5.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(A-B)\leq\mathfrak{R}(A)+\mathfrak{R}(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(A-B)\leq\mathfrak{R}(A)+\mathfrak{R}(B)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>The contraction lemma</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We state and prove a standard contraction inequality in a form that directly applies to
coordinatewise transformations of loss vectors.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Coordinatewise application)<span id="Thmdefinition4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given functions <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{i}:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{i}:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and a set <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="S6.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(A)\coloneqq\bigl\{(\phi_{1}(a_{1}),\dots,\phi_{n}(a_{n})):\ a=(a_{1},\dots,a_{n})\in A\bigr\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(A)\coloneqq\bigl\{(\phi_{1}(a_{1}),\dots,\phi_{n}(a_{n})):\ a=(a_{1},\dots,a_{n})\in A\bigr\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Rademacher contraction lemma)<span id="Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{i}:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{i}:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz with <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{i}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{i}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(\phi(A))\leq\mathbb{E}_{\sigma}\left[\sup_{a\in A}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}\,L_{i}a_{i}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(\phi(A))\leq\mathbb{E}_{\sigma}\left[\sup_{a\in A}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}\,L_{i}a_{i}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, if <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i}\leq L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i}\leq L</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(\phi(A))\leq L\,\mathfrak{R}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℜ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(\phi(A))\leq L\,\mathfrak{R}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">It suffices to prove the one-step replacement argument and then iterate over coordinates.
Fix <math id="S6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> and define, for each <math id="S6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in A</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(a)\coloneqq\sum_{i\neq k}\sigma_{i}\phi_{i}(a_{i}),\qquad v(a)\coloneqq a_{k},\qquad\psi\coloneqq\phi_{k},\quad L\coloneqq L_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>≔</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≔</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(a)\coloneqq\sum_{i\neq k}\sigma_{i}\phi_{i}(a_{i}),\qquad v(a)\coloneqq a_{k},\qquad\psi\coloneqq\phi_{k},\quad L\coloneqq L_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Condition on <math id="S6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\sigma_{i})_{i\neq k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\sigma_{i})_{i\neq k}</annotation></semantics></math> and take expectation over <math id="S6.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> only. Write</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{+}\coloneqq\sup_{a\in A}\Bigl(U(a)+\psi(v(a))\Bigr),\qquad M_{-}\coloneqq\sup_{a\in A}\Bigl(U(a)-\psi(v(a))\Bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{+}\coloneqq\sup_{a\in A}\Bigl(U(a)+\psi(v(a))\Bigr),\qquad M_{-}\coloneqq\sup_{a\in A}\Bigl(U(a)-\psi(v(a))\Bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{k}}\left[\sup_{a\in A}\Bigl(U(a)+\sigma_{k}\psi(v(a))\Bigr)\right]=\frac{1}{2}(M_{+}+M_{-})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{k}}\left[\sup_{a\in A}\Bigl(U(a)+\sigma_{k}\psi(v(a))\Bigr)\right]=\frac{1}{2}(M_{+}+M_{-}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Next, observe that</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{+}+M_{-}=\sup_{a\in A}\bigl(U(a)+\psi(v(a))\bigr)+\sup_{b\in A}\bigl(U(b)-\psi(v(b))\bigr)=\sup_{a,b\in A}\bigl(U(a)+U(b)+\psi(v(a))-\psi(v(b))\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{+}+M_{-}=\sup_{a\in A}\bigl(U(a)+\psi(v(a))\bigr)+\sup_{b\in A}\bigl(U(b)-\psi(v(b))\bigr)=\sup_{a,b\in A}\bigl(U(a)+U(b)+\psi(v(a))-\psi(v(b))\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">By Lipschitzness, <math id="S6.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(v(a))-\psi(v(b))\leq L|v(a)-v(b)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(v(a))-\psi(v(b))\leq L|v(a)-v(b)|</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{+}+M_{-}\leq\sup_{a,b\in A}\bigl(U(a)+U(b)+L|v(a)-v(b)|\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{+}+M_{-}\leq\sup_{a,b\in A}\bigl(U(a)+U(b)+L|v(a)-v(b)|\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S6.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U(a)+U(b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U(a)+U(b)</annotation></semantics></math> is symmetric in <math id="S6.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,b)</annotation></semantics></math>, we may swap <math id="S6.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(a,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(a,b)</annotation></semantics></math> if needed and remove the
absolute value in the <em id="S6.p2.6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">supremum</em>:</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{a,b\in A}\bigl(U(a)+U(b)+L|v(a)-v(b)|\bigr)=\sup_{a,b\in A}\bigl(U(a)+U(b)+L(v(a)-v(b))\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{a,b\in A}\bigl(U(a)+U(b)+L|v(a)-v(b)|\bigr)=\sup_{a,b\in A}\bigl(U(a)+U(b)+L(v(a)-v(b))\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">Expanding again as a sum of two suprema,</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{a,b\in A}\bigl(U(a)+U(b)+L(v(a)-v(b))\bigr)=\sup_{a\in A}\bigl(U(a)+Lv(a)\bigr)+\sup_{b\in A}\bigl(U(b)-Lv(b)\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{a,b\in A}\bigl(U(a)+U(b)+L(v(a)-v(b))\bigr)=\sup_{a\in A}\bigl(U(a)+Lv(a)\bigr)+\sup_{b\in A}\bigl(U(b)-Lv(b)\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p2.8.1" class="ltx_text">Denote these by <math id="S6.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}_{-}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. Then</span></p>
<table id="S6.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}(M_{+}+M_{-})\leq\frac{1}{2}(M^{\prime}_{+}+M^{\prime}_{-})=\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{k}}\left[\sup_{a\in A}\bigl(U(a)+\sigma_{k}Lv(a)\bigr)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}(M_{+}+M_{-})\leq\frac{1}{2}(M^{\prime}_{+}+M^{\prime}_{-})=\mathbb{E}_{\sigma_{k}}\left[\sup_{a\in A}\bigl(U(a)+\sigma_{k}Lv(a)\bigr)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p2.9.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, after averaging over <math id="S6.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, we may replace <math id="S6.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{k}(a_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{k}(a_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S6.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{k}a_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{k}a_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> without
increasing the quantity. Iterating this replacement for <math id="S6.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math> yields the stated bound.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmcorollary1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmcorollary1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 1</span></span><span id="Thmcorollary1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Absolute value contraction)<span id="Thmcorollary1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmcorollary1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcorollary1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A|\coloneqq\{(|a_{1}|,\dots,|a_{n}|):a\in A\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A|\coloneqq\{(|a_{1}|,\dots,|a_{n}|):a\in A\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="Thmcorollary1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(|A|)\leq\mathfrak{R}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(|A|)\leq\mathfrak{R}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Apply Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Rademacher contraction lemma). ‣ 6 The contraction lemma ‣ Does Order Matter : Connecting The Law of Robustness to Robust Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> with <math id="S6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{i}(t)=|t|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{i}(t)=|t|</annotation></semantics></math> (which is <math id="S6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz and satisfies
<math id="S6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{i}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{i}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7 </span>Coordinatewise maxima: <math id="S7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(A\vee B)\leq\mathfrak{R}(A)+\mathfrak{R}(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(A\vee B)\leq\mathfrak{R}(A)+\mathfrak{R}(B)</annotation></semantics></math></h2>

<div id="Thmdefinition5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 5</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Coordinatewise maximum)<span id="Thmdefinition5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="S7.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A\vee B\coloneqq\bigl\{a\vee b:\ a\in A,\ b\in B\bigr\},\quad\text{where}\quad(a\vee b)_{i}\coloneqq\max\{a_{i},b_{i}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where</mtext><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\vee B\coloneqq\bigl\{a\vee b:\ a\in A,\ b\in B\bigr\},\quad\text{where}\quad(a\vee b)_{i}\coloneqq\max\{a_{i},b_{i}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5</span></span><span id="Thmlemma5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Rademacher complexity of coordinatewise maxima)<span id="Thmlemma5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlemma5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, one has</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(A\vee B)\leq\mathfrak{R}(A)+\mathfrak{R}(B)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(A\vee B)\leq\mathfrak{R}(A)+\mathfrak{R}(B).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="S7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in A</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in B</annotation></semantics></math>, and note the scalar identity</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\{u,v\}=\frac{1}{2}\bigl(u+v+|u-v|\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\{u,v\}=\frac{1}{2}\bigl(u+v+|u-v|\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Applying this coordinatewise gives, for each <math id="S7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S7.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S7.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S7.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{a\in A,\ b\in B}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}\max\{a_{i},b_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{a\in A,\ b\in B}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}\max\{a_{i},b_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S7.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sup_{a,b}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}\frac{1}{2}\bigl(a_{i}+b_{i}+|a_{i}-b_{i}|\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sup_{a,b}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}\frac{1}{2}\bigl(a_{i}+b_{i}+|a_{i}-b_{i}|\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S7.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S7.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}\sup_{a\in A}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}a_{i}+\frac{1}{2}\sup_{b\in B}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}b_{i}+\frac{1}{2}\sup_{a,b}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}|a_{i}-b_{i}|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}\sup_{a\in A}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}a_{i}+\frac{1}{2}\sup_{b\in B}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}b_{i}+\frac{1}{2}\sup_{a,b}\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sigma_{i}|a_{i}-b_{i}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectations over <math id="S7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="S7.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(A\vee B)\leq\frac{1}{2}\mathfrak{R}(A)+\frac{1}{2}\mathfrak{R}(B)+\frac{1}{2}\mathfrak{R}(|A-B|)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℜ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℜ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℜ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(A\vee B)\leq\frac{1}{2}\mathfrak{R}(A)+\frac{1}{2}\mathfrak{R}(B)+\frac{1}{2}\mathfrak{R}(|A-B|).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">By Corollary <a href="#Thmcorollary1" title="Corollary 1 (Absolute value contraction). ‣ 6 The contraction lemma ‣ Does Order Matter : Connecting The Law of Robustness to Robust Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <math id="S7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(|A-B|)\leq\mathfrak{R}(A-B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(|A-B|)\leq\mathfrak{R}(A-B)</annotation></semantics></math>, and by Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4 (Translations and Minkowski sums). ‣ 5 Rademacher complexity for loss vectors ‣ Does Order Matter : Connecting The Law of Robustness to Robust Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>(c),
<math id="S7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(A-B)\leq\mathfrak{R}(A)+\mathfrak{R}(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(A-B)\leq\mathfrak{R}(A)+\mathfrak{R}(B)</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting gives <math id="S7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(A\vee B)\leq\mathfrak{R}(A)+\mathfrak{R}(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(A\vee B)\leq\mathfrak{R}(A)+\mathfrak{R}(B)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S8" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">8 </span>Application: robust squared loss</h2>

<div id="S8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix a sample <math id="S8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=((x_{i},y_{i}))_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=((x_{i},y_{i}))_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}\in[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}\in[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the class</p>
<table id="S8.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{L}\coloneqq\{f:\mathcal{X}\to[-1,1]:f\ \text{is $L$-Lipschitz}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mtext>is </mtext><mi>L</mi><mtext>-Lipschitz</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{L}\coloneqq\{f:\mathcal{X}\to[-1,1]:f\ \text{is $L$-Lipschitz}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For a function class <math id="S8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> and sample <math id="S8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, define the <em id="S8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">evaluation vectors</em></p>
<table id="S8.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}\circ S\coloneqq\{(f(x_{1}),\dots,f(x_{n})):\ f\in\mathcal{F}\}\subseteq[-1,1]^{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}\circ S\coloneqq\{(f(x_{1}),\dots,f(x_{n})):\ f\in\mathcal{F}\}\subseteq[-1,1]^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S8.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Define the squared loss <math id="S8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell(u,y)\coloneqq(u-y)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(u,y)\coloneqq(u-y)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and the robust loss <math id="S8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> as above.
Then the corresponding <em id="S8.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">loss vector classes</em> are</p>
<table id="S8.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S\coloneqq\{(\ell(f(x_{i}),y_{i}))_{i=1}^{n}:\ f\in\mathcal{B}_{L}\},\qquad\ell_{\rho}\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S\coloneqq\{(\ell_{\rho}(f;(x_{i},y_{i})))_{i=1}^{n}:\ f\in\mathcal{B}_{L}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S\coloneqq\{(\ell(f(x_{i}),y_{i}))_{i=1}^{n}:\ f\in\mathcal{B}_{L}\},\qquad\ell_{\rho}\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S\coloneqq\{(\ell_{\rho}(f;(x_{i},y_{i})))_{i=1}^{n}:\ f\in\mathcal{B}_{L}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1</span></span><span id="Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Robust loss complexity is at most twice standard squared loss)<span id="Thmproposition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every sample <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(\ell_{\rho}\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S)\leq 2\,\mathfrak{R}(\ell\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℜ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(\ell_{\rho}\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S)\leq 2\,\mathfrak{R}(\ell\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S8.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S8.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{B}_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{B}_{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, define <math id="S8.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{+},f^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{+},f^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> as in Section 1. By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (Envelopes preserve Lipschitzness). ‣ 4 Local extremal envelopes ‣ Does Order Matter : Connecting The Law of Robustness to Robust Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>,
<math id="S8.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{+},f^{-}\in\mathcal{B}_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{+},f^{-}\in\mathcal{B}_{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S8.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now define</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\coloneqq\{((f^{+}(x_{i})-y_{i})^{2})_{i=1}^{n}:\ f\in\mathcal{B}_{L}\},\qquad B\coloneqq\{((f^{-}(x_{i})-y_{i})^{2})_{i=1}^{n}:\ f\in\mathcal{B}_{L}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\coloneqq\{((f^{+}(x_{i})-y_{i})^{2})_{i=1}^{n}:\ f\in\mathcal{B}_{L}\},\qquad B\coloneqq\{((f^{-}(x_{i})-y_{i})^{2})_{i=1}^{n}:\ f\in\mathcal{B}_{L}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3 (Worst-case squared deviation is at an endpoint). ‣ 4 Local extremal envelopes ‣ Does Order Matter : Connecting The Law of Robustness to Robust Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, for each <math id="S8.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{B}_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{B}_{L}</annotation></semantics></math> the robust loss vector
<math id="S8.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="((\ell_{\rho}(f;(x_{i},y_{i})))_{i=1}^{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">((\ell_{\rho}(f;(x_{i},y_{i})))_{i=1}^{n})</annotation></semantics></math> equals the coordinatewise maximum of an element of <math id="S8.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>
and an element of <math id="S8.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\rho}\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S\subseteq A\vee B,\quad\text{so}\quad\mathfrak{R}(\ell_{\rho}\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S)\leq\mathfrak{R}(A\vee B)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>so</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\rho}\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S\subseteq A\vee B,\quad\text{so}\quad\mathfrak{R}(\ell_{\rho}\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S)\leq\mathfrak{R}(A\vee B).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 5 (Rademacher complexity of coordinatewise maxima). ‣ 7 Coordinatewise maxima: ℜ(𝐴∨𝐵)≤ℜ(𝐴)+ℜ(𝐵) ‣ Does Order Matter : Connecting The Law of Robustness to Robust Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, <math id="S8.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(A\vee B)\leq\mathfrak{R}(A)+\mathfrak{R}(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(A\vee B)\leq\mathfrak{R}(A)+\mathfrak{R}(B)</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, since <math id="S8.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{+},f^{-}\in\mathcal{B}_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{+},f^{-}\in\mathcal{B}_{L}</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have <math id="S8.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq\ell\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq\ell\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\subseteq\ell\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\subseteq\ell\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="S8.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(A)\leq\mathfrak{R}(\ell\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(A)\leq\mathfrak{R}(\ell\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S)</annotation></semantics></math> and likewise for <math id="S8.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2</span></span><span id="Thmproposition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Squared loss contracts to prediction complexity)<span id="Thmproposition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every sample <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}\in[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}\in[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(\ell\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S)\leq 4\,\mathfrak{R}(\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℜ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(\ell\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S)\leq 4\,\mathfrak{R}(\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S8.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Write <math id="S8.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S\subseteq[-1,1]^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S\subseteq[-1,1]^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each coordinate <math id="S8.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{i}(u)\coloneqq(u-y_{i})^{2}-(0-y_{i})^{2}=(u-y_{i})^{2}-y_{i}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{i}(u)\coloneqq(u-y_{i})^{2}-(0-y_{i})^{2}=(u-y_{i})^{2}-y_{i}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then <math id="S8.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{i}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{i}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and for <math id="S8.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,u^{\prime}\in[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,u^{\prime}\in[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\phi_{i}(u)-\phi_{i}(u^{\prime})|=|(u-y_{i})^{2}-(u^{\prime}-y_{i})^{2}|=|u-u^{\prime}|\cdot|u+u^{\prime}-2y_{i}|\leq|u-u^{\prime}|\cdot 4," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\phi_{i}(u)-\phi_{i}(u^{\prime})|=|(u-y_{i})^{2}-(u^{\prime}-y_{i})^{2}|=|u-u^{\prime}|\cdot|u+u^{\prime}-2y_{i}|\leq|u-u^{\prime}|\cdot 4,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">so <math id="S8.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S8.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz on <math id="S8.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S8.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S8.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, observe that adding the constant vector <math id="S8.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(y_{i}^{2})_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(y_{i}^{2})_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> does not change Rademacher
complexity (Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4 (Translations and Minkowski sums). ‣ 5 Rademacher complexity for loss vectors ‣ Does Order Matter : Connecting The Law of Robustness to Robust Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>(a)), hence</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(\ell\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S)=\mathfrak{R}(\phi(\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(\ell\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S)=\mathfrak{R}(\phi(\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S8.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Applying Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Rademacher contraction lemma). ‣ 6 The contraction lemma ‣ Does Order Matter : Connecting The Law of Robustness to Robust Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> with Lipschitz constants <math id="S8.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i}=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i}=4</annotation></semantics></math> yields
<math id="S8.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(\phi(\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S))\leq 4\,\mathfrak{R}(\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℜ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(\phi(\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S))\leq 4\,\mathfrak{R}(\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmcorollary2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmcorollary2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 2</span></span><span id="Thmcorollary2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmcorollary2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmcorollary2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmcorollary2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every sample <math id="Thmcorollary2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmcorollary2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}\in[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}\in[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S8.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{R}(\ell_{\rho}\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S)\leq 8\,\mathfrak{R}(\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℜ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℜ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{R}(\ell_{\rho}\circ\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S)\leq 8\,\mathfrak{R}(\mathcal{B}_{L}\circ S).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S8.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S8.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combine Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Robust loss complexity is at most twice standard squared loss). ‣ 8 Application: robust squared loss ‣ Does Order Matter : Connecting The Law of Robustness to Robust Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Squared loss contracts to prediction complexity). ‣ 8 Application: robust squared loss ‣ Does Order Matter : Connecting The Law of Robustness to Robust Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">9 </span>Empirical Scaling of Data-Dependent Lipschitz Lower Bounds</h2>

<div id="S9.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We aim to empirically evaluate which of the proposed scaling laws better describes the behavior observed in real-world datasets. In particular, we compare the following candidate relationships between dataset size <math id="S9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, parameter count <math id="S9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, and effective dimension <math id="S9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="S9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(n,p)\propto\sqrt{\frac{nd}{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(n,p)\propto\sqrt{\frac{nd}{p}}</annotation></semantics></math> as proposed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bubeck and Sellke, 2021</a>)</cite>, and <math id="S9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(n,p)\propto n^{1/d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(n,p)\propto n^{1/d}</annotation></semantics></math> as suggested in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. Directly computing global Lipschitz constants for deep neural networks is intractable in practice <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Scaman and Virmaux (2019)</a></cite>. Consequently, our goal is to measure a <em id="S9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">data-dependent empirical lower bound</em> and study how this quantity scales with <math id="S9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S9.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">9.1 </span>Dataset Choice and Effective Dimension</h3>

<div id="S9.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We perform experiments on the MNIST <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Deng, 2012</a>)</cite> handwritten digit dataset. Our primary motivation for selecting MNIST is consistency with the original experimental setting used in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bubeck and Sellke, 2021</a>)</cite>. Using the same dataset allows for more direct comparison between observed empirical scaling behavior and previously proposed theoretical bounds.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Additionally, MNIST is one of the few standard vision datasets for which the effective intrinsic dimension is relatively well understood. While MNIST images lie in a 784-dimensional ambient pixel space, the data is known to concentrate on a significantly lower-dimensional manifold due to strong spatial correlations and structured class semantics <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2018</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Following prior empirical Lipschitz estimation work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fazlyab et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, we therefore fix the effective dimension to <span id="S9.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">d = 10</span>. The dataset is loaded once and reused across experiments. For each experimental configuration, we construct deterministic subsets of size <math id="S9.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> using seeded random sampling without replacement. This ensures full reproducibility across runs while maintaining statistical independence across experimental configurations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">9.2 </span>Varying Parameter Count and Dataset Size</h3>

<div id="S9.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To study the joint scaling of Lipschitz behavior with dataset size <math id="S9.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and model capacity, we construct an experimental setup in which these two quantities can be varied independently while keeping all other factors fixed. In particular, we control model capacity through the number of trainable parameters <math id="S9.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, while maintaining a fixed architectural structure to preserve inductive bias.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We adopt a convolutional architecture in which the feature extraction layers are held constant across all experiments, and only the width of the fully connected layer is varied. This design ensures that low-level representations remain stable.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The architecture is given by:</p>
<ul id="S9.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S9.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S9.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Convolution (1 <math id="S9.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> 32, kernel 3<math id="S9.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>3, padding 1), followed by ReLU and MaxPool</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S9.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S9.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Convolution (32 <math id="S9.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> 64, kernel 3<math id="S9.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>3, padding 1), followed by ReLU and MaxPool</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S9.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S9.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fully connected layer: <math id="S9.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64\cdot 7\cdot 7\rightarrow\text{width}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mtext>width</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64\cdot 7\cdot 7\rightarrow\text{width}</annotation></semantics></math>, followed by ReLU</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S9.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S9.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Output layer: width <math id="S9.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> 10 logits</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The total number of trainable parameters <math id="S9.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is computed exactly for each model instance. Model capacity is varied by sweeping the hidden layer width <math id="S9.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{width}\in\{2,4,8,16,32,64,128,256,512,768\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>width</mtext><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>128</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>256</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>512</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>768</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{width}\in\{2,4,8,16,32,64,128,256,512,768\}</annotation></semantics></math>, which induces a parameter range of approximately <math id="S9.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in[2.5\times 10^{4},\;2.4\times 10^{6}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn> 2.4</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in[2.5\times 10^{4},\;2.4\times 10^{6}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Independently, we vary the dataset size <math id="S9.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\{1000,2000,\dots,10000\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1000</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2000</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>10000</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\{1000,2000,\dots,10000\}</annotation></semantics></math>. This two-dimensional sweep over <math id="S9.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n,p)</annotation></semantics></math> allows us to systematically probe how the empirical Lipschitz lower bound scales along both axes, enabling a direct comparison with the proposed theoretical scaling laws.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Since outputs are bounded in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bubeck and Sellke, 2021</a>)</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, our raw logits are passed through a hyperbolic tangent transformation <math id="S9.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{f}(x)=\tanh(f(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{f}(x)=\tanh(f(x))</annotation></semantics></math>.
This step ensures bounded outputs in <math id="S9.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S9.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.20971v1/loss_curves.png" id="S9.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/210;" width="476" height="210" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>Loss curves of models chosen at random (the other loss curves can be found in our codebase).</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">9.3 </span>Training Until Overfitting</h3>

<div id="S9.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Rather than training for a fixed number of epochs, models are trained until they enter a consistent overfitting regime. This design choice is motivated by our fundamental assumption of smooth interpolation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We therefore define overfitting using an early stopping rule. Let <math id="S9.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{test}}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mtext>test</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{test}}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> denote test loss at epoch <math id="S9.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. We track the best test loss observed so far and count consecutive epochs without improvement. Training terminates when test loss fails to improve for 10 consecutive epochs. This ensures models have entered an overfitting phase. Training uses Adam optimization, learning rate <math id="S9.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math>, cross-entropy loss, and batch size 128.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">9.4 </span>Empirical Lipschitz Lower Bound Estimation</h3>

<div id="S9.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following training, we compute a finite-sample empirical Lipschitz lower bound over the training dataset. This follows the methodology proposed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, which estimates realized sensitivity along observed data directions.</p>
</div>
<section id="S9.SS4.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">9.4.1 </span>Pairwise Finite Difference Estimation</h4>

<div id="S9.SS4.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS4.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For all pairs of training samples <math id="S9.SS4.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i},x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i},x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute class-wise local slopes: <math id="S9.SS4.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i,j,c}=\frac{|\tilde{f}_{c}(x_{i})-\tilde{f}_{c}(x_{j})|}{\|x_{i}-x_{j}\|_{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i,j,c}=\frac{|\tilde{f}_{c}(x_{i})-\tilde{f}_{c}(x_{j})|}{\|x_{i}-x_{j}\|_{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math> For each class we compute the maximum observed slope: <math id="S9.SS4.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{c}=\max_{i,j}L_{i,j,c}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{c}=\max_{i,j}L_{i,j,c}.</annotation></semantics></math> The empirical Lipschitz estimate is then <math id="S9.SS4.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathrm{emp}}=\max_{c}L_{c}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>emp</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathrm{emp}}=\max_{c}L_{c}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS4.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS4.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This quantity constitutes a lower bound on the global Lipschitz constant because it is restricted to observed sample directions rather than worst-case adversarial directions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS4.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS4.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The computation is exact over the dataset and scales as <math id="S9.SS4.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, which motivates restricting experiments to <math id="S9.SS4.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\leq 10^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\leq 10^{4}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">9.5 </span>Results</h3>

<div id="S9.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first compute the empirical Lipschitz lower bound <math id="S9.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathrm{emp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>emp</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathrm{emp}}</annotation></semantics></math> for all configurations in the <math id="S9.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n,p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n,p)</annotation></semantics></math> grid, resulting in a total of 100 measurements corresponding to all combinations of dataset sizes and model widths.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the smallest model widths (2 and 4), we observe that the empirical Lipschitz estimate evaluates to <math id="S9.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.00" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.00</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.00</annotation></semantics></math> for a small number of dataset sizes (three values of <math id="S9.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> for width 2, and two values for width 4). We hypothesize that this behavior arises from the interaction between limited model capacity and the output bounding procedure.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In particular, for these low-capacity models, the network outputs (logits) appear to be predominantly negative across certain subsets of the data. After applying the transformation <math id="S9.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{f}(x)=\tanh(f(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{f}(x)=\tanh(f(x))</annotation></semantics></math>, this leads to outputs saturating near <math id="S9.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math>. As a result, differences of the form <math id="S9.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\tilde{f}(x_{i})-\tilde{f}(x_{j})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\tilde{f}(x_{i})-\tilde{f}(x_{j})|</annotation></semantics></math> collapse to zero for many pairs of inputs, yielding an empirical Lipschitz estimate of zero. We drop these values to ensure consistency in evaluation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S9.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.20971v1/varyn.png" id="S9.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/248;" width="476" height="248" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>Lipschitz Growth vs Dataset Size (Plots chosen at random, others can be found in our codebase).</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S9.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.20971v1/vary_p.png" id="S9.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/248;" width="476" height="248" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Lipschitz Growth vs Model Parameters (Plots chosen at random, others can be found in our codebase).</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S9.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To quantify scaling behavior, we assume a power law relationship of the form <math id="S9.SS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=C\cdot n^{\alpha}\cdot p^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=C\cdot n^{\alpha}\cdot p^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S9.SS5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant, and <math id="S9.SS5.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\beta</annotation></semantics></math> capture the dependence on dataset size and model capacity respectively. Taking logarithms, this becomes <math id="S9.SS5.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log L=\log C+\alpha\log n+\beta\log p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log L=\log C+\alpha\log n+\beta\log p</annotation></semantics></math>, which allows linear estimation of the exponents.</p>
</div>
<section id="S9.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">9.5.1 </span>Method 1: Fixed-Variable Slices and Averaging</h4>

<div id="S9.SS5.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS5.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first estimate scaling exponents by isolating each variable independently. For fixed <math id="S9.SS5.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, we fit <math id="S9.SS5.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\propto n^{\alpha_{p}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∝</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\propto n^{\alpha_{p}}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding one estimate <math id="S9.SS5.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> per value of <math id="S9.SS5.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>. For fixed <math id="S9.SS5.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, we fit <math id="S9.SS5.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\propto p^{\beta_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∝</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\propto p^{\beta_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding one estimate <math id="S9.SS5.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> per value of <math id="S9.SS5.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. Since we have 10 values each of <math id="S9.SS5.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.SS5.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, this produces 10 estimates of <math id="S9.SS5.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and 10 estimates of <math id="S9.SS5.SSS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>. We then aggregate these via averaging: <math id="S9.SS5.SSS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\frac{1}{10}\sum_{p}\alpha_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>p</mi></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\frac{1}{10}\sum_{p}\alpha_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.SS5.SSS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\frac{1}{10}\sum_{n}\beta_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\frac{1}{10}\sum_{n}\beta_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. This approach allows us to verify whether scaling behavior is consistent across different slices of the experimental grid. Averaging across fixed-<math id="S9.SS5.SSS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and fixed-<math id="S9.SS5.SSS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> fits yields <math id="S9.SS5.SSS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\approx 0.163" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.163</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\approx 0.163</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.SS5.SSS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\approx 0.028" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.028</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\approx 0.028</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS5.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">9.5.2 </span>Method 2: Joint Estimation via Linear Regression</h4>

<div id="S9.SS5.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS5.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As a complementary approach, we estimate the scaling exponents jointly using multiple linear regression in log-space. Specifically, we fit the model
<math id="S9.SS5.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log L=\log C+\alpha\log n+\beta\log p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log L=\log C+\alpha\log n+\beta\log p</annotation></semantics></math>
across all 100 data points simultaneously. This method leverages the full dataset and provides a global estimate of the scaling exponents <math id="S9.SS5.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.SS5.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Fitting the joint model via ordinary least squares yields <math id="S9.SS5.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.1585\pm 0.027" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.1585</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.027</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.1585\pm 0.027</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.SS5.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0.0301\pm 0.012" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.0301</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.012</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0.0301\pm 0.012</annotation></semantics></math>, with corresponding 95% confidence intervals
<math id="S9.SS5.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in[0.105,0.212]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.105</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.212</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in[0.105,0.212]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S9.SS5.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in[0.006,0.055]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.006</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.055</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in[0.006,0.055]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Both coefficients are statistically significant (<math id="S9.SS5.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>).
The regression achieves <math id="S9.SS5.SSS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{2}=0.308" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.308</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{2}=0.308</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS5.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">9.5.3 </span>Comparsion with theoretical predictions</h4>

<div id="S9.SS5.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS5.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Combining both methods, our estimate for the growth of the Lipschitz constant is <math id="S9.SS5.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathrm{emp}}\approx C\cdot n^{0.16}\cdot p^{0.03}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>emp</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>0.16</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>0.03</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathrm{emp}}\approx C\cdot n^{0.16}\cdot p^{0.03}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS5.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.SS5.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now compare this empirical scaling with <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al. (2023)</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bubeck et al. (2021)</a></cite>: <span id="S9.SS5.SSS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Bubeck-style:</span> <math id="S9.SS5.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\propto\sqrt{\frac{nd}{p}}\sim n^{0.5}p^{-0.5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∝</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>p</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>0.5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\propto\sqrt{\frac{nd}{p}}\sim n^{0.5}p^{-0.5}</annotation></semantics></math>; <span id="S9.SS5.SSS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Wu-style:</span> <math id="S9.SS5.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\propto n^{1/d}=n^{0.1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∝</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>0.1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\propto n^{1/d}=n^{0.1}</annotation></semantics></math> (for <math id="S9.SS5.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=10</annotation></semantics></math>). Our findings show that the dependence on <math id="S9.SS5.SSS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S9.SS5.SSS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\approx 0.16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\approx 0.16</annotation></semantics></math>) is much closer to the Wu-style prediction (<math id="S9.SS5.SSS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math>) than the Bubeck-style scaling (<math id="S9.SS5.SSS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math>), while the dependence on <math id="S9.SS5.SSS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is negligible and slightly positive (<math id="S9.SS5.SSS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\approx 0.03" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.03</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\approx 0.03</annotation></semantics></math>), in stark contrast to the strong negative dependence (<math id="S9.SS5.SSS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.5</annotation></semantics></math>) predicted by Bubeck-style bounds.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S10" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">10 </span>Discussion</h2>

<div id="S10.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This is the first approach towards unifying notions of robustness, i.e., worst-case robustness and robust generalization eror as pointed out by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bubeck and Sellke, 2021</a>)</cite>. We also want to generalize our approach to Bregman Divergence losses. As seen in the experiments, there is a clear discrepancy: we perform classification with cross-entropy loss, while our theoretical results are derived for square losses. We also aim to improve the bounding of loss using local Lipschitz notions, thereby strengthening our bounds. In future versions, we also intend to use local Lipschitz constants for the radius of the cover itself. Additionally, we believe that Distributional Robustness can be linked with robust generalization, thus unifying different notions of robustness. On the empirical side, we also plan to run experiments on datasets beyond MNIST, namely CIFAR and ImageNet, thereby broadening the scope of the paper.</p>
</div>
</section>
